.\" Man page for db_importer(1)
.\" Generated from COMPLETE_CLI_OPTIONS_AND_ARGUMENTS.md
.TH DB_IMPORTER 1 "November 2026" "ETL Madness Flow" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
db_importer \- SQL Server XML pipeline, options, and config importer and exporter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B db_importer
.RI [ options ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B db_importer
is a dedicated command-line utility for migrating XML pipelines, CLI options profiles, and variable configurations into and out of Microsoft SQL Server repository tables
.RB ( dbo.flow_*_content ).
It performs idempotent upserts via SQL Server
.B MERGE INTO
statements, automatically detects and translates UTF-8 and UTF-16 (LE/BE) byte-order marks, and supports transparent AES-256-GCM encryption at rest
.RB ( FLOWENC:v1:... ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-action " op"
Database operation to execute:
.B import
(default; upserts record into target table) or
.B export
(extracts record from target table).
.TP
.B \-export
Shortcut boolean flag equivalent to
.BR "\-action export" .
.TP
.BI \-dsn " conn_string"
Connection string for the SQL Server instance (URL format
.I sqlserver://user:pass@host:1433?database=DB
or ADO/ODBC format).
.TP
.BI \-file " path"
Input XML file path when importing, or destination path when exporting.
Use
.B \-
or pass an empty string to read from
.I stdin
(import) or write to
.I stdout
(export).
Exported files written to disk are restricted to
.B 0600
permissions.
Default:
.IR github_ai_credit_usage.xml .
.TP
.BI \-name " key"
Unique logical record identifier in the target database table
.RI ( Name
column) used for upsert matching and export queries.
Default:
.IR github_ai_credit_usage .
.TP
.BI \-table " target"
Logical target table mapping:
.B pipeline
(default),
.BR options ,
or
.BR config .
See
.B TARGET TABLE MAPPINGS
below.
.TP
.BI \-desc " text"
Descriptive metadata stored in the
.I Description
column during imports.
Default:
.IR "Imported via Go importer" .
.TP
.B \-encrypted
On import: encrypts XML payload into an armored
.B FLOWENC:v1:...
envelope before upserting into SQL Server.
On export: decrypts encrypted database payloads before writing to disk or
.IR stdout .
(Encrypted database records are also auto-detected on export.)
.TP
.BI \-secure-key " key"
Passphrase or key for AES-256-GCM encryption/decryption.
Emits a security warning to
.I stderr
because command-line arguments are exposed in process listings; falls back to
.B FLOW_SECURE_KEY
or
.BR SECURE_KEY .
.TP
.BI \-key-file " path"
Path to a protected file containing the encryption/decryption key or passphrase.
Preferred over
.BR \-secure-key .
.SH TARGET TABLE MAPPINGS
The
.B \-table
flag maps to the following SQL Server repository tables and columns:
.TP
.B pipeline
Table:
.I dbo.flow_pipeline_content
\(em XML column:
.I PipelineXML
.RB ( NVARCHAR(MAX) ),
key column:
.I Name
.RB ( VARCHAR(120) ).
.TP
.B options
Table:
.I dbo.flow_options_content
\(em XML column:
.I OptionsXML
.RB ( NVARCHAR(MAX) ),
key column:
.I Name
.RB ( VARCHAR(120) ).
.TP
.B config
Table:
.I dbo.flow_config_content
\(em XML column:
.I ConfigXML
.RB ( NVARCHAR(MAX) ),
key column:
.I Name
.RB ( VARCHAR(120) ).
.SH ENCODING & SECURITY
.IP \(bu 3
.B BOM & UTF-16 Auto-Detection:
Automatically detects and decodes UTF-8 BOM
.RB ( "0xEF 0xBB 0xBF" ),
UTF-16 Little Endian BOM
.RB ( "0xFF 0xFE" ),
and UTF-16 Big Endian BOM
.RB ( "0xFE 0xFF" ).
.IP \(bu 3
.B Idempotent Upsert:
Imports execute an atomic
.B MERGE INTO
statement; existing records matching
.I Name
are updated in place.
.IP \(bu 3
.B Hardened File Permissions:
Exported files written to disk are created with mode
.B 0600
(owner read/write only).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FLOW_SECURE_KEY
Primary symmetric passphrase or key for AES-256-GCM encryption/decryption.
.TP
.B SECURE_KEY
Fallback symmetric passphrase or key if
.B FLOW_SECURE_KEY
is unset.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (record imported or exported cleanly).
.TP
.B 1
Failure (connection error, record not found on export, missing/invalid key, or I/O error).
.SH EXAMPLES
Import an XML pipeline into SQL Server:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
db_importer \\
  \-dsn "sqlserver://sa:Password123!@localhost:1433?database=ETL&trustServerCertificate=true" \\
  \-table pipeline \\
  \-name "github_billing" \\
  \-file ./pipelines/github_billing.xml \\
  \-desc "Production GitHub Billing Workflow"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Import an options profile encrypted at rest:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
db_importer \\
  \-dsn "sqlserver://sa:Password123!@localhost:1433?database=ETL&trustServerCertificate=true" \\
  \-table options \\
  \-name "OPTIONS_FINANCE" \\
  \-file ./options/finance_options.xml \\
  \-encrypted \\
  \-key-file /etc/flow/master.key
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export a pipeline to standard output and format with
.BR xmllint (1):
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
db_importer \-export \-dsn "$FLOW_DSN" \-table pipeline \-name "github_billing" \-file \- | xmllint \-\-format \-
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR flow (1),
.BR crypto_tool (1),
.BR flow-pipeline (5)
.PP
